{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Quick Start",
  "summary": "Put a region on the default cube, give it faces, and drag its button to turn the cube.",
  "order": 1,
  "practice": "../_scenes/cube.blend",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 1: Select an Item",
      "text": [
        "Select the item that you want Kneady controls for."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "01_select.mp4",
          "label": "In the viewport",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "selected": [
            "Cube"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "start": {
        "mode": "OBJECT",
        "select": []
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 2: Create a Region",
      "text": [
        "1. Open the N panel.",
        "2. Navigate to the Kneady tab.",
        "3. Press the + sign to create a Kneady region.",
        "",
        "A mesh item can carry many Kneady regions. You won't see anything until you assign a polygon selection for a region in the next step."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "02_region.mp4",
          "label": "In the viewport",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "operator": "kneady.tree_add"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 3: Give the Region Faces",
      "text": [
        "1. Click on \"Edit Faces.\"",
        "2. Select a polygon.",
        "3. Click on Assign to add the selection to your currently selected region.",
        "4. Click Done.",
        "5. Click Kneady at the top of the panel to turn Kneady on."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "03_assign.mp4",
          "label": "In the viewport",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "operator": "kneady.region_edit"
        },
        {
          "operator": "kneady.region_faces"
        },
        {
          "path": "scene.kneady_on",
          "is": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 4: Drag a Button",
      "text": [
        "1. Drag left and right on the button.",
        "2. Drag up and down on the button.",
        "",
        "Kneady has automatically assigned the rotation commands. We will select our own commands in the next tutorial, Change the Default Controls."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "04_haul.mp4",
          "label": "In the viewport",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "hovered": "Region 1",
          "object": "Cube"
        },
        {
          "operator": "kneady.drag",
          "with": {
            "target": "Cube",
            "region": 1,
            "button": 0
          },
          "moved": true
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
